.TH "RAPTOR-RENDER" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-render \- draw the diagram to PNG or SVG
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor render\fR [\-h] \-o FILE.png|FILE.svg [\-\-level LEVEL] [\-\-highlight SELECTOR] [\-\-zoom\-to SELECTOR] [\-\-theme {light,dark}] [\-\-max\-px MAX_PX] [\-\-no\-annotations] [\-\-layer {downtime\-share,lost\-capacity,advisor}] [\-n N] [\-j N] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render the diagram of MODEL to a PNG file (needs Qt) or, when FILE ends in .svg, to a plain SVG drawing (no Qt needed).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE.png|FILE.svg\fR
the image to write; the extension picks the format
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
hierarchy id to draw (0 = top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-highlight\fR \fISELECTOR\fR
draw this element highlighted: a name, an id or Kind:id (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-zoom\-to\fR \fISELECTOR\fR
frame a close\-up on these elements of the drawn level (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI{light|dark}\fR
colours (default light)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-px\fR \fIMAX_PX\fR
longest side of a PNG in pixels (default 1600)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-annotations\fR
leave out text boxes and other annotations
.TP
\fB\-\-layer\fR \fI{downtime\-share|lost\-capacity|advisor}\fR
SVG only: run the model with attribution and draw each element's share of downtime (or of lost flow) on the diagram, as the application's Show on canvas layers do; 'advisor' marks what `raptor advise` finds, without a run unless \-n is given
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-trials\fR \fIN\fR
with \-\-layer: runs to simulate (default: the model's own); with \-\-layer advisor, also run and add the run's findings
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
with \-\-layer: cores to run on
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
